PROMPT 6 — ROUTELESS SMART KIOSK AND LOCATION SYSTEM
ROLE

Act as an IoT solution architect, frontend engineer and transportation systems developer.

Continue the existing ROUTELESS project.

OBJECTIVE

Build a public touchscreen kiosk and integrate simulated GPS tracking.

SMART KIOSK

Create a dedicated kiosk interface designed for:

Raspberry Pi.
Touchscreen displays.
Public rural bus stops.
Landscape orientation.
Full-screen browser operation.

Main screen:

ROUTELESS — SMART RURAL TRAVEL

"Where do you want to go?"

Provide:

Starting village.
Current bus stop.
Destination.
FIND MY BUS.
AVAILABLE BUSES.
ALTERNATIVE ROUTES.
LIVE BUS INFORMATION.
HELP.
LANGUAGE SELECTION.
KIOSK REQUIREMENTS
Large buttons.
Large readable text.
High contrast.
Minimal typing.
English and Kannada.
Touch-friendly navigation.
Read-only access.
No access to private driver documents.
GPS SYSTEM

Implement:

Driver journey start.
Browser GPS permission.
Periodic location updates.
Trip-specific location records.
Timestamp validation.
Last-known location display.
Simulated GPS for demonstration.

When offline, queue GPS records locally.

Do not pretend simulated coordinates are real GPS.

LOCAL WI-FI

Create an integration interface for driver-to-kiosk communication.

For the prototype, provide a clearly labelled simulation or local API implementation.

Do not assume local Wi-Fi automatically provides internet access.

ACCEPTANCE TESTS
Kiosk works in full-screen mode.
Kiosk can search saved routes.
Kiosk displays bus freshness.
GPS simulation updates bus positions.
Stale GPS produces warnings.
Private information remains inaccessible.
Kiosk remains usable with saved data.

Preserve all existing modules.
